1
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:21,880
Cut.

2
00:00:21,880 --> 00:00:23,840
-Cut. Let's take a break.
-Okay.

3
00:00:34,350 --> 00:00:35,270
Are you tired?

4
00:00:35,270 --> 00:00:36,190
The shoot is not done yet.

5
00:00:36,190 --> 00:00:37,650
Hold on a little longer.

6
00:00:38,270 --> 00:00:39,570
I need to take a break.

7
00:00:47,870 --> 00:00:48,700
Please.

8
00:00:54,080 --> 00:00:55,580
Mom.

9
00:00:57,010 --> 00:00:59,750
[The late Kim Joowon]

10
00:01:10,770 --> 00:01:14,460
[Hello everyone, I'm Jung Yihyun...]

11
00:01:10,770 --> 00:01:14,190
Hello everyone, I'm Jung Yihyun.

12
00:01:14,190 --> 00:01:16,270
Starting today...

13
00:01:25,110 --> 00:01:26,320
Gah.

14
00:01:26,320 --> 00:01:29,920
I only came here because I heard
working at a columbarium is easy.

15
00:01:59,190 --> 00:02:00,860
Kang Jae-on?

16
00:02:04,190 --> 00:02:05,030
Over there!

17
00:02:05,320 --> 00:02:06,530
Over there!

18
00:02:06,530 --> 00:02:07,410
Mr. Jung.

19
00:02:07,780 --> 00:02:09,699
You posted on social media that you're
retiring from the industry—is that real?

20
00:02:09,699 --> 00:02:11,490
Why did you suddenly decide to retire?

21
00:02:11,490 --> 00:02:13,240
Does it have to do
with your mother's passing?

22
00:02:13,240 --> 00:02:14,040
Please say something.

23
00:02:14,040 --> 00:02:14,830
Please give us a statement.

24
00:02:14,830 --> 00:02:16,329
Don't you have anything to say
to your fans?

25
00:02:16,329 --> 00:02:17,370
Please say a few words.

26
00:02:17,370 --> 00:02:17,870
Excuse me.

27
00:02:17,870 --> 00:02:18,920
Excuse me!

28
00:02:19,079 --> 00:02:22,500
I'm Jung Yihyun's legal representative,
lawyer Yoo Taeseok.

29
00:02:22,500 --> 00:02:25,470
Please direct all official inquiries
to his agency.

30
00:02:26,300 --> 00:02:27,180
Let's go.

31
00:02:34,010 --> 00:02:35,980
[Hongseok]

32
00:02:37,010 --> 00:02:38,890
[Park Seonghyun]

33
00:02:42,010 --> 00:02:44,250
[Shin Yongseok] [Shin Junseop] [Ha Yosep]

34
00:02:52,800 --> 00:02:54,700
[Play Me]

35
00:03:11,550 --> 00:03:13,430
This place hasn't changed at all.

36
00:03:20,010 --> 00:03:22,850
[The Mermaid Prince]

37
00:03:28,560 --> 00:03:29,980
[The Mermaid Prince]

38
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:38,150
[To K, this script is written for you.]

39
00:03:41,150 --> 00:03:44,320
[To K, this script is written for you.]

40
00:03:45,150 --> 00:03:47,100
[Five years ago]

41
00:03:47,590 --> 00:03:48,760
Ah.

42
00:03:49,510 --> 00:03:50,840
Jung Yihyun.

43
00:03:52,300 --> 00:03:54,890
Since he's a celebrity,

44
00:03:54,890 --> 00:03:57,140
I hung out with him a few times,

45
00:03:57,140 --> 00:03:59,980
but he's actually pretty boring.

46
00:04:13,500 --> 00:04:15,800
[To K, this script is written for you.]

47
00:04:16,620 --> 00:04:18,910
Are you still thinking about him?

48
00:04:23,010 --> 00:04:24,250
[Manager Seho-hyung]

49
00:04:25,590 --> 00:04:26,750
Hello, Hyung.

50
00:04:32,340 --> 00:04:33,600
Did you find a painter?

51
00:04:36,220 --> 00:04:37,890
Take this off.

52
00:04:37,890 --> 00:04:40,350
Just paint all of this side.

53
00:04:40,350 --> 00:04:41,680
If you have any questions
or need anything,

54
00:04:41,680 --> 00:04:43,810
feel free to tell me anytime.

55
00:04:43,810 --> 00:04:45,270
Okay, got it.

56
00:04:45,270 --> 00:04:49,030
Also, make sure you leave work on time.

57
00:04:49,030 --> 00:04:51,530
If you ever run into the theater owner,

58
00:04:51,530 --> 00:04:53,450
you'll be fired immediately.

59
00:04:53,450 --> 00:04:55,620
Okay, I understand.

60
00:04:56,159 --> 00:04:57,409
But...

61
00:04:58,200 --> 00:05:01,790
Why? Why can't I run into the owner?

62
00:05:01,790 --> 00:05:04,290
Ah, could it be that this owner is...

63
00:05:06,460 --> 00:05:07,500
a bit abnormal?

64
00:05:08,750 --> 00:05:09,880
Huh?

65
00:05:11,130 --> 00:05:12,220
Ah, yes.

66
00:05:12,220 --> 00:05:13,800
He's crazy.

67
00:05:13,800 --> 00:05:17,010
So you definitely shouldn't run into him.

68
00:05:17,010 --> 00:05:18,100
Got it?

69
00:05:18,930 --> 00:05:19,970
Understood.

70
00:05:29,570 --> 00:05:30,980
I've already told

71
00:05:30,980 --> 00:05:33,400
the painter to leave work on time.

72
00:05:33,400 --> 00:05:35,320
You should also be careful
not to run into him.

73
00:05:35,320 --> 00:05:36,990
If people find out you're doing this
after announcing your retirement,

74
00:05:36,990 --> 00:05:38,200
it'll definitely cause a huge uproar.

75
00:05:38,200 --> 00:05:39,740
I know. I'll be careful.

76
00:05:40,909 --> 00:05:43,450
I know you originally wanted
to be a director,

77
00:05:43,450 --> 00:05:45,409
so I'm helping you out.

78
00:05:45,409 --> 00:05:48,920
But after you're done with this,
come back as an actor.

79
00:05:48,920 --> 00:05:53,260
There are so many fans waiting for you.
I'm also...

80
00:05:53,260 --> 00:05:54,550
one of them.

81
00:06:00,930 --> 00:06:02,310
Hyung,

82
00:06:02,810 --> 00:06:05,100
am I being too selfish?

83
00:06:12,280 --> 00:06:13,080
Hello, Hyung.

84
00:06:16,820 --> 00:06:18,320
Why did you suddenly
ask me to get a massage?

85
00:06:18,320 --> 00:06:19,950
Seho told me.

86
00:06:19,950 --> 00:06:21,870
That you haven't been
sleeping well lately.

87
00:06:21,870 --> 00:06:24,160
So I thought you could relax
and get some sleep.

88
00:06:24,160 --> 00:06:25,080
That's true.

89
00:06:28,210 --> 00:06:29,210
Just enjoy the massage.

90
00:06:29,210 --> 00:06:30,340
I need to take a call.

91
00:06:42,350 --> 00:06:44,680
I'm coming in.

92
00:07:31,480 --> 00:07:34,940
It must hurt a lot.

93
00:07:38,780 --> 00:07:39,990
Get out.

94
00:07:41,159 --> 00:07:41,990
What?

95
00:07:43,990 --> 00:07:45,450
I told you to get out.

96
00:07:57,090 --> 00:07:58,710
Stop.

97
00:07:58,710 --> 00:08:01,510
You're nothing if you're not an actor.

98
00:08:19,740 --> 00:08:21,700
Done already?

99
00:08:21,700 --> 00:08:23,760
Working two jobs a day is exhausting.

100
00:08:25,410 --> 00:08:28,540
You work four, so I can't really
complain in front of you.

101
00:08:29,660 --> 00:08:32,120
It's not tiring at all
once you get used to it.

102
00:08:32,669 --> 00:08:34,830
Wow, how did you get used to it?

103
00:08:35,880 --> 00:08:38,840
You said your dream
is to be an actor, right?

104
00:08:38,840 --> 00:08:40,630
Why do you want to be an actor?

105
00:08:45,800 --> 00:08:49,660
I made a promise with someone
to stand on stage together in the future.

106
00:08:50,470 --> 00:08:52,060
Someday,

107
00:08:54,810 --> 00:08:56,610
we must stand on stage together.

108
00:08:58,820 --> 00:08:59,530
Sure.

109
00:09:02,990 --> 00:09:05,280
Thanks to him, I've been able to hold on.

110
00:09:07,070 --> 00:09:09,160
But it's so hard just to see him.

111
00:09:10,540 --> 00:09:11,830
Oh my god.

112
00:09:16,710 --> 00:09:18,130
It's Jung Yihyun.

113
00:09:20,340 --> 00:09:22,920
The customer you just served
is Jung Yihyun.

114
00:09:25,800 --> 00:09:27,850
I was wondering
what he'd do after retiring.

115
00:09:27,850 --> 00:09:28,800
I didn't expect to see him here.

116
00:09:28,800 --> 00:09:30,890
Wh-What did you say?

117
00:09:30,890 --> 00:09:31,970
He retired.

118
00:09:33,100 --> 00:09:34,600
Didn't you know?

119
00:09:35,850 --> 00:09:37,500
[Actor Jung Yihyun Announces Retirement...
Ending His Acting Career]

120
00:09:41,480 --> 00:09:46,320
The person I met on the roof...
was Jung Yihyun?

121
00:09:50,950 --> 00:09:54,040
Sorry, Kimchi. You must be hungry.

122
00:10:05,590 --> 00:10:08,590
How could you just leave
without saying a word? I was so worried.

123
00:10:08,590 --> 00:10:10,180
Sorry, Hyung.

124
00:10:10,180 --> 00:10:12,100
You don't sound right.

125
00:10:12,100 --> 00:10:13,640
Did something happen?

126
00:10:13,640 --> 00:10:15,600
It's about Kimchi.

127
00:10:17,140 --> 00:10:20,650
I'm thinking about sending him
to a better place.

128
00:10:20,650 --> 00:10:23,070
Now that my mom is gone,

129
00:10:23,070 --> 00:10:25,440
I'm not confident
I can take good care of him.

130
00:10:25,440 --> 00:10:27,500
What nonsense are you talking about?

131
00:10:29,780 --> 00:10:30,990
Hyung.

132
00:10:32,870 --> 00:10:34,790
Maybe my mom was right—

133
00:10:36,790 --> 00:10:39,710
if I'm not an actor, I'm really nothing.

134
00:10:39,710 --> 00:10:41,790
I've already found a pet sitter.

135
00:10:41,790 --> 00:10:44,550
I know you're busy
and can't take care of Kimchi,

136
00:10:44,550 --> 00:10:46,260
so you don't need to worry.

137
00:10:46,670 --> 00:10:48,000
So, stop overthinking.

138
00:10:48,840 --> 00:10:49,570
Understood?

139
00:10:50,760 --> 00:10:51,470
Thank you.

140
00:11:03,020 --> 00:11:04,150
[Pet Sitter Guidelines]

141
00:11:06,990 --> 00:11:10,200
Pet Sitter Guidelines.

142
00:11:10,200 --> 00:11:11,570
One,

143
00:11:10,200 --> 00:11:11,450
[Pet Sitter Guidelines]

144
00:11:11,450 --> 00:11:13,750
[1. Must Poop Outside]

145
00:11:11,570 --> 00:11:13,120
the dog must poop outside.

146
00:11:14,410 --> 00:11:15,040
Two,

147
00:11:15,040 --> 00:11:17,040
beware of mites.

148
00:11:15,550 --> 00:11:17,050
[2. Beware of Mites]

149
00:11:17,040 --> 00:11:18,910
Avoid grassy areas.

150
00:11:17,050 --> 00:11:18,910
[2. Beware of Mites
(Avoid Grassy Areas)]

151
00:11:19,500 --> 00:11:20,120
Three,

152
00:11:20,120 --> 00:11:23,210
keep the leash short.

153
00:11:21,020 --> 00:11:23,140
[3. Keep Leash Short]

154
00:11:23,140 --> 00:11:24,750
[3. Keep Leash Short
(Might Lose the Dog Suddenly)]

155
00:11:23,210 --> 00:11:25,340
You might lose the dog suddenly.

156
00:11:28,090 --> 00:11:29,470
You look like a puppy.

157
00:11:30,720 --> 00:11:32,970
I guess I do.

158
00:11:35,010 --> 00:11:35,890
Yeah.

159
00:11:36,890 --> 00:11:38,450
Slow down.

160
00:11:39,150 --> 00:11:39,960
Paw.

161
00:11:43,450 --> 00:11:46,400
Other paw. That's right. Good boy.

162
00:11:46,400 --> 00:11:49,110
We're planning to build
a fake wall over there.

163
00:11:49,110 --> 00:11:50,950
The back needs to be painted.

164
00:11:50,950 --> 00:11:53,810
But the space is a bit cramped,
so please be careful.

165
00:12:59,010 --> 00:13:02,780
[I took Kimchi for a walk, and gave him a bath.
I had some time left, so I tidied up the house and made a quick meal.
I just thought you might be tired, so I decided to be a little nosy.
Make sure to eat. Food is fuel, after all.]

166
00:13:00,270 --> 00:13:01,850
I took Kimchi for a walk,

167
00:13:01,850 --> 00:13:04,310
and gave him a bath.

168
00:13:04,310 --> 00:13:06,230
I had some time left,
so I tidied up the house,

169
00:13:06,230 --> 00:13:07,430
and made a quick meal.

170
00:13:08,360 --> 00:13:11,490
I just thought you might be tired,

171
00:13:11,490 --> 00:13:14,610
so I decided to be a little nosy.

172
00:13:14,610 --> 00:13:16,700
Make sure to eat.

173
00:13:16,700 --> 00:13:19,160
Food is fuel, after all.

174
00:13:21,080 --> 00:13:23,250
Thank you.

175
00:13:25,120 --> 00:13:26,830
Say something.

176
00:13:26,830 --> 00:13:28,040
How much money did you make?

177
00:13:28,040 --> 00:13:29,550
Probably enough to buy a car, right?

178
00:13:29,550 --> 00:13:31,920
You are dating that guy
you're filming with, right?

179
00:13:31,920 --> 00:13:33,340
That's what the internet says.

180
00:13:33,340 --> 00:13:34,630
Hey!

181
00:13:34,630 --> 00:13:36,470
That's what friends are for.

182
00:13:36,470 --> 00:13:37,930
Just let us take a picture.

183
00:13:37,930 --> 00:13:40,640
If we take a funny picture of you,
we'll get a million followers.

184
00:13:40,640 --> 00:13:42,770
That's enough.

185
00:13:44,690 --> 00:13:46,350
If you have nothing better to do,

186
00:13:46,350 --> 00:13:48,690
you might as well help me clean.

187
00:13:50,940 --> 00:13:53,610
Who wants to help? Raise your hand.

188
00:13:54,570 --> 00:13:56,160
Hey, let's go.

189
00:14:03,250 --> 00:14:05,580
I did great, right?

190
00:14:05,580 --> 00:14:07,420
Wasn't it super cool?

191
00:14:09,250 --> 00:14:10,670
You're like a puppy.

192
00:14:11,960 --> 00:14:13,380
What?

193
00:14:14,840 --> 00:14:16,220
A puppy?

194
00:14:16,220 --> 00:14:17,590
Hey!

195
00:14:18,260 --> 00:14:19,550
Wait for me!
